Practical philosophy

        (1) the presence throughout the cosmos of a safehold highly fit to secure
          the long-term survival of mind-bearing populations
            : ad `long-term` : over periods on the scale of cosmogonal time,
              as opposed to the (relatively short) scale of geogenic time
                : re `scale of cosmogonal time`
                  see `stability on the longer ${same}` @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec
                : re `\(relatively short\) scale of geogenic time`
                  see `the scope.+not restricted to.+the ${same}`s @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec
            : re `(a safehold.+to secure the.+survival of) (mind)-bearing (populations)`p
              see `${1} ${3} of beings \(like us\) that have ${2}`p @ ~/work/safehold/40.observation.brec
        (2) by a truth of practical logic, absent knowledge of whether ∃ a ground (stable ground)
          and, if so, what it consists in (ground knowledge), that knowledge is itself
          a ground (the default ground)
            : re `^*\(\d+\) (.+)`s see `^*argue\+ that, ${same}`p @ default/._/text.notes.brec
